-- Q3364: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): In a reverse acquisition under ASC 805, the legal acquirer (which issued shares) is the accounting acquiree. Post-combination financial statements are issued under the legal acquirer''s name but reflect the accounting acquirer''s (legal acquiree''s) historical financial data, with the legal acquirer''s results included only from the acquisition date.
Wrong (B): The legal acquiree is the accounting acquirer, so its historical financials are carried forward, but they are presented under the legal acquirer''s name, not the acquiree''s.
Wrong (C): Combined historical financials are not presented; only the accounting acquirer''s pre-acquisition history is used.
Wrong (D): The legal acquirer''s historical financials alone would ignore the accounting acquirer''s continuity, which is the foundation of reverse acquisition reporting.$EXPL$
