-- Q3414: Interfund Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): A residual equity transfer is a permanent transfer of fund balance from one fund to another, typically when a fund is being closed. Under GASB standards, it is classified as an interfund transfer and reported as other financing sources/uses with no repayment expectation.
